		<orm:ModelNotes>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_48737C18-1ACB-4CF7-8460-0878FAB3FB7B">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - General</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_3BFB3AE6-6FED-40A8-8EB0-27B517CDBCAA">
				<orm:Text>Final CHECK - verify all data types related to value types</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_E5343E91-F5A3-4890-9ACE-06862D55E81D">
				<orm:Text>This part of the model is missing in PUS-C clause 5...</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_15F64C11-A542-4519-9A85-03C3E6A53DD4">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Scope and observables</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_C8BBCBA0-FBC7-45AC-850A-42EF0D2438E4">
				<orm:Text>to support PUS 6.6.2.1.1, 6.13.2.1.1</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_1095F5F2-FA89-4236-B2F5-841307883AC5" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_8F3ADDD7-EF3F-4621-A4FC-62F5E07C8FBF">
				<orm:Text>to support e.g. PUS 6.6.2.2a</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_F3E4B909-EAC4-4BAE-A144-31ADE4E5AC8F" />
					<orm:FactType ref="_48D94BA7-D349-450A-AF01-A2AC8D934581" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_F9F7446C-12FA-4FB9-B456-00BE0323636D">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Subservice type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_4DB4FB93-376D-48D2-B169-596789865392">
				<orm:Text>If needed, we could still :
1/ fully derive &quot;ServiceTypeID has MessageSubtypeID&quot; [via the path ServiceTypeID is of MessageType that has MessageSubtypeID), 
2/ objectified that relation to get the MessageTypeID and 
3/ fully derive that MessageType has MessageTypeID.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_7DD2CA36-3846-4175-9A88-4B3AB7936E80">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Message type - General</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_08075DEB-CEC8-4C50-81EB-C7A97BE061D7">
				<orm:Text>ToDO</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_CE541CD4-291D-4279-8B47-76D6E81AB725" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_DAD931E3-51D4-463C-825D-B187366D3A68">
				<orm:Text>PUSC.7.4.4.2d</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_8542A283-353F-4CC3-A929-F0D13FCDB0C8" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_C7F57A47-C235-41DA-AA24-F9F716AFE84F">
				<orm:Text>CCSDS Space Packet</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_BCB28D9F-053C-4E94-97C0-3812C7E4AEE7">
				<orm:Text>PUSC.7.4.3.1</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_0542DF3C-65A5-416C-8D6F-3831131BFCF4" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_E671C17D-CEDA-47CB-95BB-8081B0C116FE">
				<orm:Text>telemetry, telecommand</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_C279F0CA-D6AF-4E3A-B863-053B3D280A60" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_5C60D9F5-4436-4148-BB20-482ED9C689E9">
				<orm:Text>ISO standard 16-bits checksum, CRC standard 16-bits checksum</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_1A6F3DE2-E0A7-415B-944D-BC0BD0E1E770" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_2D4B6A57-3782-4B6C-8F3C-855AD452516E">
				<orm:Text>Open issues:
- A complete set of request type related ASN1 structures implies possibly 
merging the request type argument slots 
with all possbily combination of instruction type argument slots.
This is the purpose of this derived fact type. 
Let's populate some examples to see what is required and how such derivation can be done</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_BB7BA45B-D0E5-4F44-9C28-6563B4044132">
				<orm:Text>PUSC.7.4.3.2d &amp; e</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_8542A283-353F-4CC3-A929-F0D13FCDB0C8" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_57674D3D-9060-4B18-AB34-A7055D11952A">
				<orm:Text>The arguments slots represented as ASN1 structures are ok for chapter 8.
But we mgiht still need to produce the requirements for chapter 6 as:
- a  list of simple arguments or arrays or record as shown in E-70-31 and 32.
TO be further assessed.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_4C271A5A-8029-4A4E-8B02-554E1773EAF4">
				<orm:Text>Not specified in clause 5 (TBC)</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_C000A31B-F5CE-4445-89E0-C6B44E9B812A" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_B411280F-B0F8-4A98-8A6A-E06BFA7C916E">
				<orm:Text>PUSC.5.3.3.2e</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_6B2E3DB5-E0F0-4756-8988-FB81EC79B98C" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_BDAAFBE0-B68E-4A4E-AEAB-73BC123001B0">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Message type - Request type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_D75306C1-80FB-4C43-A37D-172152DB95BA">
				<orm:Text>This is entered as a semiderived fact as most of the instruction structures will be derived from their arguments. 
Some complex structures (e.g. with dependencies) may need to be asserted.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_6F9791D6-1515-4C35-B93C-EEB8B65B7F10" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_AD64C353-EEC9-4A9B-8559-026C874CEF7B">
				<orm:Text>A deduced packet type at mission/service/message tailoring should point to a packet field. 
This ternary (TBC) fact type is not yet specified.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_DD10A906-A8B5-4BC0-BED5-30FEF031A196" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_2BB18702-8A40-43A3-9577-4E82955241DC">
				<orm:Text>Should be mapped to EXPL when merging</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_044FB759-7CF2-4C81-8C81-0753D0083E5D" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_883A75DB-25FB-47E0-907E-CB12F90A140B">
				<orm:Text>At PUS level, the PFC is usually not specified. 
PUS requirement 7.3.1.x asks for PFC when declaring the Service.
See also CR.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_2BD45C34-044C-4899-A1DC-2687EB243667" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_941BEDF2-F2F8-41A7-B7E0-8FA7204A15E8">
				<orm:Text>This Packet Field Code only addresses the raw value.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_1909A033-03E6-4EF5-8A69-5493941E71D1" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_997E2A00-2940-440E-A651-BAAD84777656">
				<orm:Text>The contents of this diagram are highly redundant with similar information in the E-70-31 model. 
This needs to be carefully merged.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_EDC5A352-E14E-44BA-8D6E-61B09F3F3D06">
				<orm:Text>e.g. N1 shall be set to 0</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_B9905798-9FE4-4F42-AFAF-6B41D23BD74B" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_5E8731FC-1155-4E28-8556-0E421F6850A6">
				<orm:Text>PUS Foundation Model allows a single request to hold
a number of different InstructionTypes. However, PUS C
interface standard assumes that there is a single &quot;general&quot; 
packet structure for each RequestType, and there is
a &quot;master instruction&quot; defining the packet, and 
&quot;slave instructions&quot; which use the same structure, but with some
contraints. E.g. &quot;instruction to enable a specific X&quot; uses a packet
with a size determinant &quot;N&quot; and a list of &quot;Xs&quot;,
but may share the same packet with &quot;instruction to enable all Xs&quot;,
which has the size determinant &quot;N&quot; set to 0 and consequently a 
&quot;zero sized&quot; (empty, non-existent) list of &quot;Xs&quot;.
One such example is TC[15,1]. Such contraints are not visible 
within the Chapter 8 table, but within further (c, d, ...) Chapter 8
per request requirements.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_93FBF837-FC1A-4BDC-898C-BCD62538AACC" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_3768DAC5-E84A-4920-A826-F8387086DABD">
				<orm:Text>e.g. &quot;n&quot;, to be used as ACN size determinant</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_88B9ED7E-84E9-4DA2-AC70-21E60F84FD7A" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_092C3958-060C-46D6-B496-1A507DC73188">
				<orm:Text>e.g. &quot;n INSTRUCTION-COUNT []&quot;, to be used within TC ACN</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_8A6BCE1E-3389-4634-BF1A-1ABF4BDC5BEA" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_6C47140E-97D0-4F75-8A7C-9C20C859C1D5">
				<orm:Text>e.g. &quot;INSTRUCTION-COUNT ::= INTEGER (0..255)&quot;, to be used as instruction count type definition.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_9CD5E56D-60B5-43D9-B9F9-01847257A65D" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_62E8508E-8B20-47B8-B516-4C63BF8A2311">
				<orm:Text>This fact links an instruction with the structure used to present the repetition 
of said instruction when it allows multiples in its request.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_474204FF-6762-4E79-9009-7ACA46EA4F90" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_E68FC32F-E1AD-47DD-AEA9-5062F433C228">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Instruction type and ASN1 issues</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_E7EA3136-C5F6-4EF9-B31D-C926203A08B1">
				<orm:Text>Open issue: The completion of execution verification report 
may contain a number of &quot;progress notifications&quot;.
This concept is still to be modelled, and was detected to be problematic during the PUS-C training material perparation.
To further assess.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:SetComparisonConstraint ref="_B5BE53BB-83F6-46EE-8613-35806A343198" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_1F2E7F9A-C36C-4848-AC04-DA13B4F47FCB">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Message type - Report type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_FC935784-46AF-489C-86AD-92A164C165BD">
				<orm:Text>NotificationTypePurpose is introduced to allow documenting notifications which have no reporting data. 
It has no counterpart in the foundation model.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_48F4CB5D-3458-47B1-AA20-F4796AC423E3" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_91D2BEAD-5649-4D0A-84DF-BB9EB38510D6">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Message type - Report type (additional)</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_CDD04EFA-F16C-49AB-9D8D-367E84DF5B1B">
				<orm:Text>PUS CR: change requirements 6.11.9.1, 6.11.10.1, 6.22.11.1, 6.22.12.1 
by information only since these requirements are &quot;redundant&quot;. 
Keep the mandatory constraint on role played by Capability type in capability type directly define transaction type.
Reported as change request in TN1.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_F4D63B19-C586-41B1-9439-4C39714CB76F">
				<orm:Text>A tree capability type is a hierarchically structured, 
meaning that in the set of directly defined capability type,
there is exactly one top parent capability type 
that is either implied or to be declared and 
each other capability type are organised in subhierarchies.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_B1E3ADD4-ACC6-4470-B414-2F5AA1F8A6FF">
				<orm:Text>Each realization of the inclusive-or capability type demands 
the realization of at least one capability type 
directly defined by the compound capability type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_0F6702CD-9077-4A28-8549-BDD94D9A554D">
				<orm:Text>Each realization of the exclusive-or capability type demands 
the realization of exactly one capability type 
directly defined by the compound capability type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_50538307-6114-4B2E-8407-EEA72EA7A7E3">
				<orm:Text>Note: There are a number of missing constraints (and derivation parts) 
to ensure that only rights configurations are accepted by the model.
If a capability type is member of a inclusive-or capability type, 
it can only depend (pre-require/implied/exclude) of other members
of this group.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_B4AC255A-783F-4C45-BAF8-1E576CCDE9E4" />
					<orm:FactType ref="_4A055535-D04C-40F2-82C7-EE2B7E8B020E" />
					<orm:FactType ref="_32080DE7-BB6B-4F24-A1B0-6C2E6E2D731B" />
					<orm:FactType ref="_47A53700-BACB-4DF7-A096-D2AAD41ED9E2" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_08F0DA6C-4CC0-4A39-A550-7076F9AEC419">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Capability type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_71850167-2AD6-4438-88CB-46F6F1FE043D">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Transaction type - General</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_8E7BE4F6-44E3-4375-B4E8-C99FCED9AA3C">
				<orm:Text>*Transaction type involves message type if and only if
that transaction type is some autonomous data reporting transaction type that involves some autonomous data report type that is that message type
or that transaction type is some event reporting transaction type that involves some event report type that is that message type
or that transaction type is some request verification transaction type that involves some request verification report type that is that message type
or that transaction type is some request related transaction type that involves some response type that is that message type
or involves some request type that is that message type.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_FCC19D6E-3A1A-41F7-92A5-0B98262E3E21">
				<orm:Text>Generic service type abstraction - Transaction type - Request related transaction type</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_48ECECF4-AF70-4985-AB85-D9A07CD53800">
				<orm:Text>Failure code should always uniquely identify a single onboard condition within an application process.
The same failure code can be used by many request types for exactly the same meaning.
A failure code might only be used for one ore more request types but not obligatory by all...

a failure code specified for the Mission cannot be reused by an APID or a RequestType.
With the failure code, one shall be able to uniquely identify :
a failure code defined for the full mission,
a failure code that combined with the APID means something
a failure code that combined with the RequestType ID means something.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_81E02494-8865-4092-A1EF-1FD568D402DE">
				<orm:Text>This model, associated with request type and instruction type might be overdoing.
It need to be verified with the standardized request and instrucitons failure conditions and possibly simplified
(e.g. why having a during instruction execution condition at instruction type level. 
Such condition might still be relevant at instruction level...</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_79487DD6-141A-4589-9AB3-7500CECE87FA">
				<orm:Text>Change Request : There is a problem with PUS-C.
CLause 5.3.5.2.3g foresees a code for successful command verification 
but clause 8 does not...
Currently the model does not model such code. Reported as change request in TN1.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_4C504023-FE51-4868-9A05-B7B1D32B5D11">
				<orm:Text>OnBoardCondition might need to be further developed</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_2E1ACC0A-D320-4240-853D-C7EEE230E724">
				<orm:Text>This fact type allows modelling the data associated to a given failure code. 
Is that approach sufficient or do we need a complete structure capability?
Should we also model the associated ASN1structure?
CAUTION: This fact type is not generated in the relational model because the SystemObjectProperty objectified fact type is derived. This fact needs to be added manually !</orm:Text>
