			<orm:ModelNote id="_B14A659B-AE8D-420D-A5D4-90B8A64EB3C1">
				<orm:Text>The output of the Compiler for e.g. list of event definitions shall be checked for compliance with the related application process event definitions...
Once the compiler model is presented, we can also create the List of Possible Values for the selection of the Lexical values...</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_DD95C980-1490-4AB8-8E77-D9EC70FFB62E">
				<orm:Text>Declared as IndependentObjectType and keep it with Error (i.e. due to absence of Preferred Identifier.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_6F8BCE90-0C96-474D-BB1F-4AE32BC79805" />
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_D9DDEEF8-C81A-430E-8BAF-4990F5FEBC29" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_835D971D-3299-4702-84D9-C729C93A37A0">
				<orm:Text>The event definition reference consists in 
- the identifier of the application process that hosts the event reporting subservice generating the event,
- the event definition identifier.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_FD5917B1-ED3E-4805-BF0E-517DB3CA4F1B" />
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_D33101DB-17C0-4836-9436-278913F1C4AE" />
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_C7993CD4-40A2-4FA8-B57E-7A76A9181145" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_7FCF7AFA-88A4-444F-BFCE-75FC0A84A6FF">
				<orm:Text>While it could be argued that all parameters have a definition, 
only those parameters that have an explicit parameter definition as per
service 20 are involved in this fact type.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_5AEEACA9-4CD1-4C1F-A808-B1E0E039CC4B" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_444A6345-C071-4309-9A21-2AA69BFEBCEA">
				<orm:Text>Create CR to PUS to introduce the concept of ConfigurableOnboardParameter associated to Service 20 (remove the concept OnboardParameterDefinition.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_1E185A0D-7252-472F-856E-6C37DC1680FE">
				<orm:Text>We could further subtypes the StructuredMemories (static and dynamic based) and also the related definition</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_3A35BCEF-00FB-4B32-88A6-D93D8FF3D078">
				<orm:Text>This fact type is a population element of the &quot;Subservice provides CapabilityType&quot; fact type,
which is only added here to specify the constraint.</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:FactType ref="_FDF80B77-885C-4317-837C-B75DD6E8C50B" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_78BCE901-56A8-441C-AD95-2CCAB918AC3D">
				<orm:Text>Note that 5.4.5 already describes most of the file system properties</orm:Text>
				<orm:ReferencedBy>
					<orm:ObjectType ref="_A26A09DA-7DED-4933-920B-69E0326047DD" />
				</orm:ReferencedBy>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_F314D7B8-B56D-4F16-8E8D-CA7C33ACB815">
				<orm:Text>This is the application ID of the parameter report definition</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_ED3C8CE6-8967-4911-8D0B-F0A5D9765AB3">
				<orm:Text>UPDATE TAKING INTO ACCOUNT THE CHANGES ON SERVICE11</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_F5F5585D-4D54-451A-8362-7D844398BB1D">
				<orm:Text>DO THE SAME AS ST14</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
			<orm:ModelNote id="_90FAFAC6-8F64-459A-9165-A422D3BFDD95">
				<orm:Text>FreeFBM: this model was exported from FreeFBM. Not in NORMA's form: 6
derivation rules as NORMA paths (kept as informal rules). Where it
concerns one element, the element's note (NORMA's Notes window) says
more, after “FreeFBM:”.</orm:Text>
			</orm:ModelNote>
		</orm:ModelNotes>
